        "old_string": "# rp1-eval-project\n\nA minimal Bun project for testing rp1 agent evaluations.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts    - Main entry point\n  utils.ts    - Utility functions\n```",
        "new_string": "# rp1-eval-project\n\nA minimal Bun project for testing rp1 agent evaluations.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter\n- `bun run validate` - Validate YAML file syntax\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n### YAML Validator\n\nValidates YAML file syntax by parsing the specified file and reporting success or failure.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\nbun run validate <file-path>\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n\n- `file-path` - Path to the YAML file to validate\n\n**Exit Codes:**\n\n| Code | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| 0 | YAML file is valid |\n| 1 | Validation failed or error occurred |\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\n# Validate a YAML configuration file\nbun run validate config.yaml\n# Output: Valid YAML: config.yaml\n\n# Validate a file with a syntax error\nbun run validate invalid.yaml\n# Output: Syntax error at line 15: unexpected token\n\n# Attempt to validate a non-existent file\nbun run validate missing.yaml\n# Output: Error: File not found: missing.yaml\n\n# Run without arguments (shows usage)\nbun run validate\n# Output: Usage: bun run validate <file-path>\n```\n\n## Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts       - Main entry point\n  utils.ts       - Utility functions\n  validate.ts    - YAML validator CLI\n  yaml-parser.ts - Custom YAML parser\n```"
      },
