        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-01-22\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design specifies a command-line YAML syntax validator for the rp1-eval-project. The validator accepts a file path argument, parses the YAML content using a custom-built parser, and reports success or failure with appropriate error messages and exit codes.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Layer\"]\n        A[validate.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Parser[\"Parser Layer\"]\n        B[yaml-parser.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph System[\"System Layer\"]\n        C[File System]\n        D[Process/Exit]\n    end\n\n    A --> B\n    A --> C\n    A --> D\n    B --> E[YamlLexer]\n    B --> F[YamlParser]\n```\n\n**Design Principles:**\n- Single responsibility: Separate CLI handling from parsing logic\n- Zero dependencies: All parsing logic implemented from scratch\n- Pattern alignment: Follow existing project structure and conventions\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Structure\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| CLI Entry Point | `src/validate.ts` | Argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting |\n| YAML Parser | `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Lexical analysis and parsing of YAML content |\n\n### 2.2 Component Interaction\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate.ts\n    participant FS as File System\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate config.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments\n    CLI->>FS: Check file exists\n    alt File not found\n        CLI->>User: Error: File not found\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    CLI->>FS: Read file contents\n    CLI->>Parser: parseYaml(content)\n    alt Parse success\n        Parser->>CLI: { success: true, data }\n        CLI->>User: Valid YAML\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(0)\n    else Parse failure\n        Parser->>CLI: { success: false, error, line }\n        CLI->>User: Syntax error at line N: message\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 YAML Parser Module (`src/yaml-parser.ts`)\n\nThe custom YAML parser implements a two-phase approach: lexical analysis followed by parsing.\n\n#### 3.1.1 Supported YAML Syntax\n\n| Syntax Element | Example | Supported |\n|----------------|---------|-----------|\n| Scalar values | `key: value` | Yes |\n| Quoted strings | `key: \"value\"` or `key: 'value'` | Yes |\n| Multi-line strings | `key: \\|` or `key: >` | Yes |\n| Numbers | `count: 42` | Yes |\n| Booleans | `enabled: true` | Yes |\n| Null values | `value: null` or `value: ~` | Yes |\n| Mappings (objects) | `key:\\n  nested: value` | Yes |\n| Sequences (arrays) | `- item1\\n- item2` | Yes |\n| Inline sequences | `items: [a, b, c]` | Yes |\n| Inline mappings | `obj: {key: value}` | Yes |\n| Comments | `# comment` | Yes |\n| Anchors/Aliases | `&anchor`, `*alias` | No |\n| Tags | `!tag` | No |\n| Multi-document | `---` separator | No |\n\n#### 3.1.2 Parser Interface\n\n```typescript\n// Types\ninterface YamlParseSuccess {\n  success: true;\n  data: YamlValue;\n}\n\ninterface YamlParseError {\n  success: false;\n  error: string;\n  line: number;\n  column?: number;\n}\n\ntype YamlParseResult = YamlParseSuccess | YamlParseError;\n\ntype YamlValue =\n  | string\n  | number\n  | boolean\n  | null\n  | YamlValue[]\n  | { [key: string]: YamlValue };\n\n// Main function\nfunction parseYaml(content: string): YamlParseResult;\n```\n\n#### 3.1.3 Lexer Design\n\nThe lexer tokenizes YAML input into a stream of tokens:\n\n```typescript\nenum TokenType {\n  KEY,           // key identifier before colon\n  COLON,         // :\n  STRING,        // quoted or unquoted string value\n  NUMBER,        // numeric value\n  BOOLEAN,       // true/false\n  NULL,          // null/~\n  DASH,          // - for list items\n  LBRACKET,      // [\n  RBRACKET,      // ]\n  LBRACE,        // {\n  RBRACE,        // }\n  COMMA,         // ,\n  PIPE,          // | for literal block\n  GT,            // > for folded block\n  NEWLINE,       // line break\n  INDENT,        // indentation increase\n  DEDENT,        // indentation decrease\n  EOF,           // end of file\n}\n\ninterface Token {\n  type: TokenType;\n  value: string;\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n}\n```\n\n#### 3.1.4 Parser State Machine\n\nThe parser maintains a state stack for handling nested structures:\n\n```typescript\ninterface ParserState {\n  indent: number;       // Current indentation level\n  context: 'root' | 'mapping' | 'sequence' | 'inline-mapping' | 'inline-sequence';\n  expectingValue: boolean;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 CLI Entry Point (`src/validate.ts`)\n\n#### 3.2.1 Command Interface\n\n```\nUsage: bun run validate <file-path>\n\nArguments:\n  file-path    Path to the YAML file to validate\n\nExit Codes:\n  0            YAML file is valid\n  1            Validation failed or error occurred\n```\n\n#### 3.2.2 CLI Implementation Structure\n\n```typescript\n// Main entry point\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n\n  // Validate arguments\n  if (args.length === 0) {\n    printUsage();\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const filePath = args[0];\n\n  // Check file existence\n  if (!await fileExists(filePath)) {\n    console.error(`Error: File not found: ${filePath}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  // Read file\n  const content = await readFile(filePath);\n\n  // Parse YAML\n  const result = parseYaml(content);\n\n  // Output result\n  if (result.success) {\n    console.log(`Valid YAML: ${filePath}`);\n    process.exit(0);\n  } else {\n    console.error(`Syntax error at line ${result.line}: ${result.error}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 3.2.3 Error Message Formats\n\n| Scenario | Output Format |\n|----------|---------------|\n| No arguments | `Usage: bun run validate <file-path>` |\n| File not found | `Error: File not found: {path}` |\n| Valid YAML | `Valid YAML: {path}` |\n| Syntax error | `Syntax error at line {N}: {message}` |\n\n### 3.3 Data Model\n\nNo persistent data storage required. The parser produces an in-memory representation that is discarded after validation.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Justification |\n|-------|------------|---------------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Project standard (existing) |\n| Language | TypeScript | Project standard (existing) |\n| File I/O | Bun built-in fs | No external dependencies |\n| Testing | bun:test | Project standard (existing) |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Effort |\n|---|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| 1 | YAML Parser Core | Implement lexer and parser in `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Medium |\n| 2 | CLI Entry Point | Implement `src/validate.ts` with argument handling | Small |\n| 3 | Package.json Update | Add \"validate\" script | Trivial |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - YAML parser has no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2] - CLI entry point depends on parser being complete\n3. [T3] - Package.json update depends on CLI entry point\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface dependency: CLI imports and uses parseYaml function)\n- T3 -> T2 (Build dependency: Script references validate.ts entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------|-----------|\n| Parser unit tests | HIGH | Core business logic - validates YAML syntax |\n| CLI integration tests | MEDIUM | Verifies end-to-end behavior |\n| Edge case tests | HIGH | YAML has many syntax variations |\n\n### 7.2 Test Plan\n\n#### 7.2.1 Parser Unit Tests (`src/yaml-parser.test.ts`)\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Empty string | `\"\"` | Success, null value |\n| Simple key-value | `key: value` | Success, {key: \"value\"} |\n| Nested mapping | `a:\\n  b: c` | Success, {a: {b: \"c\"}} |\n| Simple sequence | `- a\\n- b` | Success, [\"a\", \"b\"] |\n| Mixed nesting | `items:\\n  - a\\n  - b` | Success, {items: [\"a\", \"b\"]} |\n| Quoted strings | `key: \"val: ue\"` | Success, {key: \"val: ue\"} |\n| Numbers | `count: 42` | Success, {count: 42} |\n| Booleans | `flag: true` | Success, {flag: true} |\n| Comments | `# comment\\nkey: val` | Success, {key: \"val\"} |\n| Inline array | `items: [a, b]` | Success, {items: [\"a\", \"b\"]} |\n| Inline object | `obj: {a: 1}` | Success, {obj: {a: 1}} |\n| Invalid: bad indent | `a:\\nb: c` | Error at line 2 |\n| Invalid: unclosed quote | `key: \"value` | Error at line 1 |\n| Invalid: bad colon | `key value` | Error at line 1 |\n\n#### 7.2.2 CLI Integration Tests (`src/validate.test.ts`)\n\n| Test Case | Setup | Expected |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Valid file | Temp file with valid YAML | Exit 0, success message |\n| Invalid file | Temp file with invalid YAML | Exit 1, error with line |\n| Missing file | Non-existent path | Exit 1, file not found |\n| No arguments | No args | Exit 1, usage message |\n\n### 7.3 Test NOT Designed\n\n| Category | Reason |\n|----------|--------|\n| Bun file system behavior | Framework testing |\n| process.argv parsing | Runtime behavior |\n| Console output formatting | Library feature |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Package.json Changes\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate\": \"bun run src/validate.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 8.2 No Build/Deploy Changes\n\n- No compilation step needed (Bun runs TypeScript directly)\n- No environment variables required\n- No configuration files needed\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | CLI Commands | N/A | Document new validate command usage |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|\n| D1 | Parser architecture | Two-phase (lexer + parser) | Cleaner separation, easier error reporting |\n| D2 | File structure | New entry point `validate.ts` | Follows existing `index.ts` pattern |\n| D3 | Parser module location | `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Follows existing `utils.ts` pattern |\n| D4 | Error reporting | Line number only (no column) | Simpler implementation, sufficient for most cases |\n| D5 | Result type | Discriminated union | Type-safe success/error handling |\n| D6 | Unsupported features handling | Parse error | Clear feedback for users |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: YAML Syntax Reference\n\n### Supported Grammar (Simplified BNF)\n\n```\ndocument    := value\nvalue       := scalar | mapping | sequence\nscalar      := string | number | boolean | null\nmapping     := (key COLON value NEWLINE)+\nsequence    := (DASH value NEWLINE)+\nkey         := string\nstring      := QUOTE char* QUOTE | unquoted-char+\nnumber      := DIGIT+ (DOT DIGIT+)?\nboolean     := 'true' | 'false'\nnull        := 'null' | '~'\n```\n\n### Indentation Rules\n\n- Indentation uses spaces only (tabs are errors)\n- Consistent indentation within a block (typically 2 spaces)\n- Nested structures must be indented more than parent\n"
