        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 4 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 1.5 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-22\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator that accepts a file path argument, parses YAML content using a custom-built parser (no external dependencies), and reports success or failure with appropriate error messages and exit codes.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - YAML parser has no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2] - CLI entry point depends on parser being complete\n3. [T3] - Package.json update depends on CLI entry point\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface dependency: CLI imports and uses parseYaml function)\n- T3 -> T2 (Build dependency: Script references validate.ts entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Parser Layer\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML parser with lexer and parser in `src/yaml-parser.ts` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-yaml-parser-module-srcyaml-parserts](design.md#31-yaml-parser-module-srcyaml-parserts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Lexer tokenizes YAML input into stream of tokens (KEY, COLON, STRING, NUMBER, BOOLEAN, NULL, DASH, brackets, PIPE, GT, NEWLINE, INDENT, DEDENT, EOF)\n    - [ ] Parser implements two-phase approach: lexical analysis followed by parsing\n    - [ ] Parser maintains state stack with indent level, context (root/mapping/sequence/inline-mapping/inline-sequence), and expectingValue flag\n    - [ ] Supports scalar values (strings, numbers, booleans, null)\n    - [ ] Supports quoted strings (single and double quotes)\n    - [ ] Supports multi-line strings (pipe `|` and folded `>` syntax)\n    - [ ] Supports mappings (nested objects with indentation)\n    - [ ] Supports sequences (arrays with dash syntax)\n    - [ ] Supports inline sequences `[a, b, c]` and inline mappings `{key: value}`\n    - [ ] Supports comments (lines starting with `#`)\n    - [ ] Returns discriminated union type: `YamlParseSuccess` or `YamlParseError` with line number\n    - [ ] Rejects tabs in indentation as errors\n    - [ ] Unit tests pass for all cases in design section 7.2.1\n\n### CLI Layer\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI entry point in `src/validate.ts` with argument handling and file I/O `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-entry-point-srcvalidatets](design.md#32-cli-entry-point-srcvalidatets)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Accepts file path as command-line argument via `process.argv`\n    - [ ] Displays usage message when no arguments provided: `Usage: bun run validate <file-path>`\n    - [ ] Checks file existence before attempting to read\n    - [ ] Outputs `Error: File not found: {path}` for non-existent files\n    - [ ] Reads file content using Bun built-in fs\n    - [ ] Calls `parseYaml(content)` from yaml-parser module\n    - [ ] Outputs `Valid YAML: {path}` on successful parse\n    - [ ] Outputs `Syntax error at line {N}: {message}` on parse failure\n    - [ ] Returns exit code 0 on success, exit code 1 on any failure\n    - [ ] Integration tests pass for all cases in design section 7.2.2\n\n### Configuration\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Add validate script to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#81-packagejson-changes](design.md#81-packagejson-changes)\n\n    **Effort**: 15 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `scripts` section includes `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate.ts\"`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate config.yaml` invokes the validator\n    - [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Create documentation for README.md - CLI Commands `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: CLI Commands\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New CLI Commands section created in README.md\n    - [ ] Documents `bun run validate <file-path>` command usage\n    - [ ] Includes example invocations and expected output\n    - [ ] Documents exit codes (0 for success, 1 for failure)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n- [ ] REQ-001: Running `bun run validate config.yaml` passes the file path to the validator\n- [ ] REQ-002: Non-existent file paths produce a clear \"file not found\" error message\n- [ ] REQ-003: Parser correctly handles scalars, key-value mappings, lists, nested structures, and comments\n- [ ] REQ-004: Valid YAML files produce output indicating success (e.g., \"Valid YAML\")\n- [ ] REQ-005: Invalid YAML produces error message with line number (e.g., \"Syntax error at line 15: ...\")\n- [ ] REQ-006: Exit code 0 on valid YAML, exit code 1 on invalid YAML or errors\n- [ ] REQ-007: package.json dependencies remain unchanged after implementation\n- [ ] STORY-001: GIVEN a valid YAML file exists at \"config.yaml\" WHEN I run `bun run validate config.yaml` THEN I see a success message confirming the file is valid\n- [ ] STORY-002: GIVEN a YAML file with a syntax error on line 10 WHEN I run the validate command THEN I see an error message indicating the problem at line 10\n- [ ] STORY-003: GIVEN no file exists at \"missing.yaml\" WHEN I run `bun run validate missing.yaml` THEN I see an error message stating the file was not found\n- [ ] STORY-004: GIVEN a valid YAML file WHEN the validate command completes THEN the exit code is 0 AND GIVEN an invalid YAML file WHEN the validate command completes THEN the exit code is non-zero\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Parser unit tests passing (`src/yaml-parser.test.ts`)\n- [ ] CLI integration tests passing (`src/validate.test.ts`)\n- [ ] Documentation updated (README.md)\n- [ ] No new npm dependencies added\n"
