        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-01-22\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design describes a zero-dependency YAML syntax validator CLI command for the Bun-based TypeScript project. The validator will parse YAML files and report syntax errors with line numbers and descriptions, supporting single file, multiple file, and glob pattern validation.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Layer\"]\n        A[validate-yaml command]\n        B[Argument Parser]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Core Layer\"]\n        C[Validator Orchestrator]\n        D[YAML Syntax Parser]\n        E[Error Formatter]\n    end\n\n    subgraph IO[\"I/O Layer\"]\n        F[File Reader]\n        G[Glob Resolver]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Output[\"Output\"]\n        H[stdout - success]\n        I[stderr - errors]\n        J[Exit Codes]\n    end\n\n    A --> B\n    B --> C\n    C --> D\n    C --> F\n    C --> G\n    D --> E\n    C --> H\n    E --> I\n    C --> J\n```\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|-----------|\n| YAML Parsing | Inline implementation | REQ-007 mandates no new dependencies |\n| CLI Parsing | Manual argv processing | No external libraries allowed; follows existing pattern |\n| Glob Support | Bun.Glob built-in | Native Bun capability, not an npm dependency |\n| File Structure | Flat src/ layout | Matches existing project structure |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph \"src/\"\n        A[yaml-validator.ts<br/>CLI Entry Point]\n        B[yaml-parser.ts<br/>Syntax Validation]\n        C[yaml-validator.test.ts<br/>Tests]\n    end\n\n    A --> B\n    C -.-> A\n    C -.-> B\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| CLI Entry | `src/yaml-validator.ts` | Parse arguments, orchestrate validation, handle output |\n| YAML Parser | `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Tokenize and validate YAML syntax |\n| Tests | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | Unit and integration tests |\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as yaml-validator.ts\n    participant Glob as Bun.Glob\n    participant FS as Bun.file\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n    participant Out as stdout/stderr\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate-yaml [files...]\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments\n\n    alt Glob Pattern\n        CLI->>Glob: Resolve pattern\n        Glob-->>CLI: File list\n    end\n\n    loop Each file\n        CLI->>FS: Read file content\n        FS-->>CLI: Content or error\n\n        alt File read error\n            CLI->>Out: Error to stderr\n        else File read success\n            CLI->>Parser: validateYaml(content)\n            Parser-->>CLI: ValidationResult\n\n            alt Valid\n                CLI->>Out: Success to stdout\n            else Invalid\n                CLI->>Out: Errors to stderr\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    CLI->>User: Exit code (0/1/2)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 YAML Parser Module\n\nThe parser implements a lightweight YAML syntax validator focusing on detecting structural errors rather than full parsing. This approach minimizes complexity while meeting the requirement of accurate syntax error detection.\n\n#### Core Types\n\n```typescript\n// src/yaml-parser.ts\n\nexport interface YamlError {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: YamlError[];\n}\n\nexport interface ParserState {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  indentStack: number[];\n  inMultilineString: boolean;\n  stringDelimiter: string | null;\n}\n```\n\n#### Parsing Strategy\n\nThe parser uses a line-by-line tokenization approach:\n\n1. **Line Scanning**: Process input line by line, tracking position\n2. **Indent Tracking**: Maintain indent stack for structure validation\n3. **Token Recognition**: Identify keys, values, lists, multi-line strings\n4. **Error Collection**: Accumulate all errors (continue after finding errors)\n\n#### Key Validation Rules\n\n| Rule | Validation | Error |\n|------|------------|-------|\n| Indentation | Consistent spaces (not mixed tabs/spaces) | \"Inconsistent indentation\" |\n| Key Syntax | Valid key format before colon | \"Invalid key syntax\" |\n| String Quotes | Matching quote pairs | \"Unterminated string\" |\n| List Items | Proper dash-space prefix | \"Invalid list item\" |\n| Document Markers | Valid --- and ... placement | \"Invalid document marker\" |\n| Duplicate Keys | Same key at same level | \"Duplicate key\" |\n\n#### Public API\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Validate YAML syntax without fully parsing the document.\n * @param content - YAML content string\n * @returns ValidationResult with validity status and any errors\n */\nexport function validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;\n\n/**\n * Validate YAML syntax for multi-document files.\n * @param content - YAML content string (may contain ---)\n * @returns ValidationResult with errors across all documents\n */\nexport function validateMultiDocYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;\n```\n\n### 3.2 CLI Module\n\n#### Argument Structure\n\n```typescript\n// src/yaml-validator.ts\n\ninterface CliOptions {\n  files: string[];\n  quiet: boolean;\n  help: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface FileValidationResult {\n  path: string;\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: YamlError[];\n  fileError?: string;  // For file access errors\n}\n```\n\n#### Command Syntax\n\n```\nbun run validate-yaml [options] <file...>\n\nArguments:\n  file...              YAML file paths or glob patterns\n\nOptions:\n  -q, --quiet          Only output errors, suppress success messages\n  -h, --help           Show help message\n\nExit Codes:\n  0                    All files valid\n  1                    One or more files have validation errors\n  2                    Invalid arguments or file access errors\n```\n\n#### CLI Flow\n\n```typescript\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  // 1. Parse arguments\n  const options = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n\n  if (options.help) {\n    printHelp();\n    process.exit(0);\n  }\n\n  if (options.files.length === 0) {\n    console.error(\"Error: No files specified\");\n    printUsage();\n    process.exit(2);\n  }\n\n  // 2. Resolve files (including globs)\n  const resolvedFiles = await resolveFiles(options.files);\n\n  if (resolvedFiles.length === 0) {\n    console.error(\"Error: No files matched\");\n    process.exit(2);\n  }\n\n  // 3. Validate each file\n  const results = await validateFiles(resolvedFiles);\n\n  // 4. Output results\n  outputResults(results, options.quiet);\n\n  // 5. Exit with appropriate code\n  const hasValidationErrors = results.some(r => !r.valid && !r.fileError);\n  const hasFileErrors = results.some(r => r.fileError);\n\n  if (hasFileErrors) {\n    process.exit(2);\n  } else if (hasValidationErrors) {\n    process.exit(1);\n  } else {\n    process.exit(0);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 File Operations\n\n#### File Reading\n\n```typescript\nasync function readYamlFile(path: string): Promise<{ content?: string; error?: string }> {\n  try {\n    // Security: Validate path\n    const normalizedPath = normalizePath(path);\n    if (!isLocalPath(normalizedPath)) {\n      return { error: \"Only local file paths are allowed\" };\n    }\n\n    const file = Bun.file(normalizedPath);\n\n    if (!await file.exists()) {\n      return { error: `File not found: ${path}` };\n    }\n\n    const content = await file.text();\n    return { content };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { error: `Cannot read file: ${err.message}` };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Glob Resolution\n\n```typescript\nasync function resolveGlob(pattern: string): Promise<string[]> {\n  const glob = new Bun.Glob(pattern);\n  const matches: string[] = [];\n\n  for await (const path of glob.scan({ dot: false })) {\n    if (path.endsWith('.yaml') || path.endsWith('.yml')) {\n      matches.push(path);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return matches;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.4 Error Formatting\n\n```typescript\nfunction formatError(file: string, error: YamlError): string {\n  return `${file}:${error.line}:${error.column}: ${error.message}`;\n}\n\nfunction formatFileError(file: string, message: string): string {\n  return `${file}: ${message}`;\n}\n\n// Example output:\n// config/app.yaml:15:3: Invalid indentation - expected 4 spaces, got 3\n// config/db.yaml: File not found\n```\n\n### 3.5 Security Considerations\n\n| Concern | Mitigation |\n|---------|------------|\n| Path Traversal | Normalize paths, reject paths with `..` outside working directory |\n| Remote URLs | Check for protocol prefixes (http://, ftp://), reject non-local |\n| File Size | Check file size before reading, reject files > 10MB |\n| Content Execution | Parser only tokenizes, never evaluates content |\n\n```typescript\nfunction isLocalPath(path: string): boolean {\n  // Reject URLs\n  if (/^[a-z]+:\\/\\//i.test(path)) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Resolve to absolute and check it's within allowed scope\n  const resolved = resolve(path);\n  const cwd = process.cwd();\n\n  return resolved.startsWith(cwd) || !path.includes('..');\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Justification |\n|-------|------------|---------------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language |\n| File I/O | Bun.file | Native Bun API, no dependencies |\n| Glob | Bun.Glob | Native Bun API, no dependencies |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing test framework |\n| YAML Parsing | Custom inline | REQ-007 no-dependency constraint |\n\n### Dependencies Impact\n\n```diff\n// package.json - NO CHANGES\n{\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/bun\": \"latest\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Effort | Priority |\n|---|-----------|-------------|--------|----------|\n| T1 | YAML Tokenizer | Core syntax validation logic | High | Must Have |\n| T2 | CLI Argument Parser | Parse --quiet, --help, file args | Low | Must Have |\n| T3 | File Reader | Bun.file wrapper with error handling | Low | Must Have |\n| T4 | Error Formatter | Format errors for stderr output | Low | Must Have |\n| T5 | Glob Handler | Resolve glob patterns to file list | Low | Could Have |\n| T6 | Validator Orchestrator | Main CLI combining all components | Medium | Must Have |\n| T7 | Tests | Unit and integration tests | Medium | Must Have |\n\n### Implementation Order\n\n1. **Phase 1 - Core** (T1, T4): YAML parser and error formatting\n2. **Phase 2 - CLI** (T2, T3, T6): CLI infrastructure and orchestration\n3. **Phase 3 - Enhancement** (T5): Glob pattern support\n4. **Phase 4 - Quality** (T7): Comprehensive testing\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2, T3, T4, T5] - All core modules can be built independently\n2. [T6] - Orchestrator requires all core modules\n3. [T7] - Tests require parser and orchestrator\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T6 -> [T1, T2, T3, T4, T5] (Orchestrator integrates all modules)\n- T7 -> [T1, T6] (Tests validate parser and end-to-end behavior)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T6 -> T7\n\n```\n     +----+     +----+     +----+\n     | T2 |     | T3 |     | T4 |\n     +----+     +----+     +----+\n        \\          |          /\n         \\         |         /\n          v        v        v\n+----+    +---------------+     +----+\n| T1 | -->|      T6       |<--- | T5 |\n+----+    +---------------+     +----+\n                  |\n                  v\n              +----+\n              | T7 |\n              +----+\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Categories\n\n| Category | Coverage Target | Rationale |\n|----------|-----------------|-----------|\n| YAML Parser Unit Tests | 90%+ | Core business logic |\n| CLI Integration Tests | Key paths | End-to-end validation |\n| Error Handling Tests | All error types | Reliability |\n| Edge Cases | Documented edge cases | Robustness |\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Type | Value | Include |\n|-----------|-------|---------|\n| Valid YAML detection | HIGH - core requirement | Yes |\n| Invalid YAML error messages | HIGH - core requirement | Yes |\n| Line number accuracy | HIGH - user-facing | Yes |\n| Multi-document support | HIGH - BR-004 | Yes |\n| Exit code correctness | HIGH - CI integration | Yes |\n| Glob pattern expansion | MEDIUM - Could Have feature | Yes |\n| Edge cases (empty files, large files) | MEDIUM - robustness | Yes |\n| Path traversal prevention | HIGH - security | Yes |\n\n### Test Cases\n\n```typescript\n// src/yaml-validator.test.ts\n\ndescribe(\"yaml-parser\", () => {\n  describe(\"validateYaml\", () => {\n    test(\"valid simple YAML returns no errors\", () => {\n      const result = validateYaml(\"key: value\\n\");\n      expect(result.valid).toBe(true);\n      expect(result.errors).toHaveLength(0);\n    });\n\n    test(\"invalid indentation reports line number\", () => {\n      const yaml = \"parent:\\n child: value\\n\";  // Missing space\n      const result = validateYaml(yaml);\n      expect(result.valid).toBe(false);\n      expect(result.errors[0].line).toBe(2);\n    });\n\n    test(\"unterminated string reports error\", () => {\n      const yaml = 'key: \"unclosed\\n';\n      const result = validateYaml(yaml);\n      expect(result.valid).toBe(false);\n      expect(result.errors[0].message).toContain(\"Unterminated\");\n    });\n\n    test(\"empty file is valid (BR-002)\", () => {\n      const result = validateYaml(\"\");\n      expect(result.valid).toBe(true);\n    });\n\n    test(\"multi-document YAML is supported (BR-004)\", () => {\n      const yaml = \"doc1: a\\n---\\ndoc2: b\\n\";\n      const result = validateMultiDocYaml(yaml);\n      expect(result.valid).toBe(true);\n    });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"yaml-validator CLI\", () => {\n  test(\"exits 0 for valid file\");\n  test(\"exits 1 for invalid YAML\");\n  test(\"exits 2 for missing file\");\n  test(\"--quiet suppresses success messages\");\n  test(\"--help shows usage\");\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### Package.json Script Addition\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/yaml-validator.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Usage Examples\n\n```bash\n# Single file\nbun run validate-yaml config.yaml\n\n# Multiple files\nbun run validate-yaml config.yaml settings.yaml\n\n# Glob pattern\nbun run validate-yaml \"config/**/*.yaml\"\n\n# Quiet mode (for CI)\nbun run validate-yaml --quiet config.yaml\n\n# Direct execution\nbun src/yaml-validator.ts config.yaml\n```\n\n### CI Integration Example\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/validate.yml\n- name: Validate YAML files\n  run: bun run validate-yaml --quiet \"config/**/*.yaml\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | README.md | Scripts | N/A | Add validate-yaml script documentation |\n| add | (none required) | - | - | Self-documenting via --help |\n\n### README Update\n\n```markdown\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run validate-yaml <files>` - Validate YAML file syntax\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML Parsing Approach | Inline syntax validator | REQ-007 no-dependency constraint | External library (rejected), Bundled library (rejected) |\n| D2 | CLI Argument Parsing | Manual argv processing | No dependencies allowed; simple requirements | yargs (rejected - dependency), commander (rejected - dependency) |\n| D3 | File Structure | Flat src/ with 2 new files | Matches existing minimal project structure | Nested folders (overkill for size) |\n| D4 | Glob Implementation | Bun.Glob | Built into Bun runtime, not npm dependency | node-glob (rejected - dependency), manual impl (unnecessary) |\n| D5 | Error Output | stderr with file:line:col format | Standard linter format, CI-friendly | JSON output (overly complex for CLI) |\n| D6 | Multi-file Handling | Continue on error, report all | Better UX for batch validation | Stop on first error (less useful) |\n| D7 | Test Framework | bun:test | Existing project pattern | Jest (would add dependency) |\n\n---\n\n## AFK Mode: Auto-Selected Technology Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Source | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Codebase | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Codebase | Existing project language |\n| Test Framework | bun:test | Codebase | Existing test pattern in utils.test.ts |\n| File I/O API | Bun.file | Bun docs | Native Bun API, avoids dependencies |\n| Glob API | Bun.Glob | Bun docs | Native Bun API, avoids dependencies |\n| Module Pattern | ES Modules | tsconfig.json | moduleResolution: bundler |\n| Strict Mode | Enabled | tsconfig.json | strict: true |\n| File Layout | Flat src/ | Codebase | Matches existing structure |\n"
