        "content": "# Design Decisions: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Created**: 2026-01-22\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML Parsing Approach | Inline syntax validator | REQ-007 mandates no new dependencies; Bun has no built-in YAML parser; inline implementation provides control and meets constraint | External library like js-yaml (rejected - violates no-dependency constraint), Bundled/vendored library (rejected - still counts as dependency code to maintain) |\n| D2 | CLI Argument Parsing | Manual process.argv processing | No external dependencies allowed; argument structure is simple (files, --quiet, --help); follows existing pattern in src/index.ts | yargs (rejected - npm dependency), commander (rejected - npm dependency), minimist (rejected - npm dependency) |\n| D3 | File Structure | Flat src/ layout with yaml-validator.ts and yaml-parser.ts | Matches existing minimal project structure (utils.ts, index.ts pattern); avoids over-engineering for a 2-module feature | Nested src/yaml-validator/ folder (rejected - overkill for project size), Single file (rejected - poor separation of concerns) |\n| D4 | Glob Implementation | Bun.Glob built-in API | Native Bun runtime capability, not an npm package dependency; well-tested implementation | node-glob npm package (rejected - adds dependency), fast-glob (rejected - adds dependency), Manual glob implementation (rejected - unnecessary when Bun provides it) |\n| D5 | Error Output Format | stderr with file:line:column: message format | Standard linter/compiler format familiar to developers; easily parsed by IDEs and CI systems; follows Unix convention (errors to stderr) | JSON structured output (rejected - overly complex for CLI use case), Simple text (rejected - less useful for IDE integration) |\n| D6 | Multi-file Error Handling | Continue validation, report all errors | Better user experience for batch validation; allows fixing multiple files in one pass; exit code still reflects overall status | Stop on first error (rejected - less useful for batch operations) |\n| D7 | Test Framework | bun:test | Existing project test pattern; no additional dependencies; native Bun integration | Jest (rejected - would add devDependency), Vitest (rejected - would add devDependency), Mocha (rejected - would add devDependency) |\n| D8 | Validation Scope | Syntax validation only, not schema validation | Explicit in requirements scope; reduces complexity significantly; schema validation would require additional specification | Full YAML parsing (rejected - more complexity than needed), Schema validation (rejected - out of scope per REQ) |\n| D9 | Exit Code Strategy | 0=success, 1=validation error, 2=file/arg error | REQ-004 explicitly specifies this; standard Unix convention; allows CI to distinguish error types | Single non-zero for all errors (rejected - less informative), Exit on first error (rejected - loses batch info) |\n| D10 | YAML Version Support | YAML 1.1 and 1.2 core syntax | Covers vast majority of YAML files in use; 1.2 is current standard; 1.1 compatibility for legacy files | YAML 1.2 only (rejected - would break some legacy files), Full spec compliance (rejected - extreme complexity for inline impl) |\n\n## AFK Mode: Auto-Selected Technology Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Source | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Codebase analysis | package.json scripts use `bun`, devDependencies include @types/bun |\n| Language | TypeScript | Codebase analysis | All source files are .ts, tsconfig.json present |\n| Test Framework | bun:test | Codebase analysis | Existing utils.test.ts uses `import { describe, expect, test } from \"bun:test\"` |\n| Module System | ES Modules | tsconfig.json | \"module\": \"ESNext\", \"type\": \"module\" in package.json |\n| Strict Mode | Enabled | tsconfig.json | \"strict\": true already configured |\n| File I/O | Bun.file API | Bun runtime default | Native async file API, no dependencies needed |\n| Glob Support | Bun.Glob | Bun runtime default | Native glob support, no npm package needed |\n| Output Pattern | console.log/console.error | Codebase analysis | Existing index.ts uses console.log for output |\n| Argument Access | process.argv | Codebase analysis | Existing index.ts uses process.argv[2] pattern |\n| Test Co-location | Same directory as source | Codebase analysis | utils.test.ts alongside utils.ts |\n\n## Risk Decisions\n\n| Risk | Decision | Mitigation |\n|------|----------|------------|\n| Inline YAML parser may not handle all edge cases | Accept partial coverage | Document known limitations; focus on common YAML patterns; add tests for edge cases |\n| Performance with large files | Accept synchronous processing | File size check before processing; document 10MB limit |\n| Security (path traversal) | Implement path validation | Normalize paths; reject URLs; validate within working directory |\n\n## Deferred Decisions\n\n| Topic | Reason | When to Decide |\n|-------|--------|----------------|\n| stdin input support | Out of scope for v1 | Future enhancement if requested |\n| JSON output format | Not in requirements | If CI tools request structured output |\n| Watch mode | Not in requirements | If continuous validation requested |\n| Config file support | Not in requirements | If default options needed |\n"
