        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 8 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 4 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-22\n\n## Overview\n\nA zero-dependency YAML syntax validator CLI command for the Bun-based TypeScript project. The validator parses YAML files and reports syntax errors with line numbers and descriptions, supporting single file, multiple file, and glob pattern validation.\n\n**Important Limitation**: Hypothesis testing revealed that inline YAML parsing catches only ~11% of errors compared to js-yaml. However, per REQ-007, we must proceed without adding dependencies. The implementation will provide best-effort syntax checking with clearly documented limitations.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2, T3, T4, T5] - All core modules can be built independently\n2. [T6] - Orchestrator requires all core modules\n3. [T7] - Tests require parser and orchestrator\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T6 -> [T1, T2, T3, T4, T5] (Orchestrator integrates all modules)\n- T7 -> [T1, T6] (Tests validate parser and end-to-end behavior)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T6 -> T7\n\n```\n     +----+     +----+     +----+\n     | T2 |     | T3 |     | T4 |\n     +----+     +----+     +----+\n        \\          |          /\n         \\         |         /\n          v        v        v\n+----+    +---------------+     +----+\n| T1 | -->|      T6       |<--- | T5 |\n+----+    +---------------+     +----+\n                  |\n                  v\n              +----+\n              | T7 |\n              +----+\n```\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Core Modules\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML Tokenizer with best-effort syntax validation logic `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-yaml-parser-module](design.md#31-yaml-parser-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 8 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Create `src/yaml-parser.ts` with `YamlError`, `ValidationResult`, and `ParserState` types\n    - [ ] Implement `validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult` function\n    - [ ] Implement `validateMultiDocYaml(content: string): ValidationResult` function for multi-document support (BR-004)\n    - [ ] Validate indentation consistency (detect mixed tabs/spaces)\n    - [ ] Detect unterminated strings (matching quote pairs)\n    - [ ] Detect invalid list items (proper dash-space prefix)\n    - [ ] Detect duplicate keys at same level\n    - [ ] Validate document markers (--- and ...) placement\n    - [ ] Return line and column numbers for all detected errors\n    - [ ] Empty files return valid result (BR-002)\n    - [ ] Document known limitations in code comments (only catches ~11% of errors that js-yaml would catch)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI argument parser for --quiet, --help, and file arguments `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-module](design.md#32-cli-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Parse `-q` and `--quiet` flags for quiet mode\n    - [ ] Parse `-h` and `--help` flags for help display\n    - [ ] Collect remaining arguments as file paths/patterns\n    - [ ] Return structured `CliOptions` object with `files`, `quiet`, and `help` properties\n    - [ ] Handle edge cases: no arguments, only flags, mixed flags and files\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement file reader with Bun.file wrapper and error handling `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-file-operations](design.md#33-file-operations)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Implement `readYamlFile(path: string)` returning `{ content?: string; error?: string }`\n    - [ ] Validate paths to prevent path traversal attacks (reject `..` outside working directory)\n    - [ ] Reject remote URLs (http://, ftp://, etc.)\n    - [ ] Check file existence before reading\n    - [ ] Enforce 10MB file size limit\n    - [ ] Return appropriate error messages for each failure case (BR-003)\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Implement error formatter for stderr output in file:line:col format `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-error-formatting](design.md#34-error-formatting)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Implement `formatError(file: string, error: YamlError): string` returning `file:line:col: message` format\n    - [ ] Implement `formatFileError(file: string, message: string): string` for file access errors\n    - [ ] Output format is compatible with standard linter conventions\n    - [ ] Error messages are human-readable and actionable (REQ-003)\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Implement glob handler using Bun.Glob for pattern resolution `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-file-operations](design.md#33-file-operations)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Implement `resolveGlob(pattern: string): Promise<string[]>` using Bun.Glob\n    - [ ] Filter results to only .yaml and .yml files (BR-001)\n    - [ ] Exclude dot files by default\n    - [ ] Handle patterns matching no files gracefully\n    - [ ] Support recursive patterns (e.g., `**/*.yaml`)\n\n### Integration\n\n- [ ] **T6**: Implement validator orchestrator as main CLI entry point `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-module](design.md#32-cli-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Create `src/yaml-validator.ts` as CLI entry point\n    - [ ] Integrate argument parser, file reader, glob handler, YAML parser, and error formatter\n    - [ ] Implement `printHelp()` showing command syntax and options\n    - [ ] Implement `printUsage()` for error cases\n    - [ ] Exit code 0 when all files pass validation (REQ-004)\n    - [ ] Exit code 1 when one or more files fail validation (REQ-004)\n    - [ ] Exit code 2 for invalid arguments or file access errors (REQ-004)\n    - [ ] Quiet mode suppresses success messages but shows errors (REQ-006)\n    - [ ] Continue validation through all files even if some fail (REQ-002)\n    - [ ] Add `validate-yaml` script to package.json\n\n### Quality\n\n- [ ] **T7**: Implement comprehensive unit and integration tests `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Create `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` using bun:test\n    - [ ] Test valid simple YAML returns no errors\n    - [ ] Test invalid indentation reports correct line number\n    - [ ] Test unterminated string reports error with \"Unterminated\" message\n    - [ ] Test empty file is valid (BR-002)\n    - [ ] Test multi-document YAML is supported (BR-004)\n    - [ ] Test CLI exits 0 for valid file\n    - [ ] Test CLI exits 1 for invalid YAML\n    - [ ] Test CLI exits 2 for missing file\n    - [ ] Test --quiet suppresses success messages\n    - [ ] Test --help shows usage\n    - [ ] Test path traversal prevention (security)\n    - [ ] Test glob pattern expansion\n    - [ ] Document test coverage limitations (inline parser catches ~11% of errors)\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Add `bun run validate-yaml <files>` to Scripts section\n    - [ ] Include brief description of command purpose\n    - [ ] Note limitations of inline parser (best-effort syntax checking)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n### REQ-001: Single File Validation\n- [ ] Given a valid YAML file path, when validation is run, then success message is displayed and exit code is 0\n- [ ] Given an invalid YAML file path, when validation is run, then error message with file path is displayed and exit code is non-zero\n- [ ] Given a file with invalid YAML syntax, when validation is run, then error details including line number are displayed\n\n### REQ-002: Multiple File Validation\n- [ ] Given multiple file paths, when validation is run, then each file is validated independently\n- [ ] Given a mix of valid and invalid files, when validation is run, then all results are reported and exit code reflects overall status\n- [ ] Validation continues through all files even if some fail\n\n### REQ-003: Error Reporting\n- [ ] Error messages include the file path\n- [ ] Error messages include the line number where the error was detected\n- [ ] Error messages include a human-readable description of the syntax problem\n- [ ] Error output is written to stderr\n\n### REQ-004: Exit Code Behavior\n- [ ] Exit code 0 when all files pass validation\n- [ ] Exit code 1 when one or more files fail validation\n- [ ] Exit code 2 when command-line arguments are invalid or files cannot be read\n\n### REQ-005: Glob Pattern Support\n- [ ] Given a glob pattern like \"config/*.yaml\", when validation is run, then all matching files are validated\n- [ ] Given a pattern matching no files, when validation is run, then appropriate message is displayed\n\n### REQ-006: Quiet Mode\n- [ ] Given quiet flag is set and files are valid, when validation is run, then no output is produced\n- [ ] Given quiet flag is set and files are invalid, when validation is run, then only error messages are output\n\n### REQ-007: No New Dependencies\n- [ ] package.json dependencies section remains unchanged after implementation\n- [ ] package.json devDependencies section remains unchanged after implementation\n- [ ] All YAML parsing is done using built-in capabilities or inline code\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Tests pass with documented coverage\n- [ ] Documentation updated with limitation notes\n- [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n"
