# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command

**Feature ID**: yaml-validator
**Version**: 1.0.0
**Status**: Draft
**Created**: 2026-01-22

---

## 1. Design Overview

This design describes a zero-dependency YAML syntax validator CLI command for the Bun-based TypeScript project. The validator will parse YAML files and report syntax errors with line numbers and descriptions, supporting single file, multiple file, and glob pattern validation.

### High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph CLI["CLI Layer"]
        A[validate-yaml command]
        B[Argument Parser]
    end

    subgraph Core["Core Layer"]
        C[Validator Orchestrator]
        D[YAML Syntax Parser]
        E[Error Formatter]
    end

    subgraph IO["I/O Layer"]
        F[File Reader]
        G[Glob Resolver]
    end

    subgraph Output["Output"]
        H[stdout - success]
        I[stderr - errors]
        J[Exit Codes]
    end

    A --> B
    B --> C
    C --> D
    C --> F
    C --> G
    D --> E
    C --> H
    E --> I
    C --> J
```

### Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
|----------|--------|-----------|
| YAML Parsing | Inline implementation | REQ-007 mandates no new dependencies |
| CLI Parsing | Manual argv processing | No external libraries allowed; follows existing pattern |
| Glob Support | Bun.Glob built-in | Native Bun capability, not an npm dependency |
| File Structure | Flat src/ layout | Matches existing project structure |

---

## 2. Architecture

### Component Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "src/"
        A[yaml-validator.ts<br/>CLI Entry Point]
        B[yaml-parser.ts<br/>Syntax Validation]
        C[yaml-validator.test.ts<br/>Tests]
    end

    A --> B
    C -.-> A
    C -.-> B
```

### Component Responsibilities

| Component | File | Responsibility |
|-----------|------|----------------|
| CLI Entry | `src/yaml-validator.ts` | Parse arguments, orchestrate validation, handle output |
| YAML Parser | `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Tokenize and validate YAML syntax |
| Tests | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | Unit and integration tests |

### Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant CLI as yaml-validator.ts
    participant Glob as Bun.Glob
    participant FS as Bun.file
    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts
    participant Out as stdout/stderr

    User->>CLI: bun run validate-yaml [files...]
    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments

    alt Glob Pattern
        CLI->>Glob: Resolve pattern
        Glob-->>CLI: File list
    end

    loop Each file
        CLI->>FS: Read file content
        FS-->>CLI: Content or error

        alt File read error
            CLI->>Out: Error to stderr
        else File read success
            CLI->>Parser: validateYaml(content)
            Parser-->>CLI: ValidationResult

            alt Valid
                CLI->>Out: Success to stdout
            else Invalid
                CLI->>Out: Errors to stderr
            end
        end
    end

    CLI->>User: Exit code (0/1/2)
```

---

## 3. Detailed Design

### 3.1 YAML Parser Module

The parser implements a lightweight YAML syntax validator focusing on detecting structural errors rather than full parsing. This approach minimizes complexity while meeting the requirement of accurate syntax error detection.

#### Core Types

```typescript
// src/yaml-parser.ts

export interface YamlError {
  line: number;
  column: number;
  message: string;
}

export interface ValidationResult {
  valid: boolean;
  errors: YamlError[];
}

export interface ParserState {
  line: number;
  column: number;
  indentStack: number[];
  inMultilineString: boolean;
  stringDelimiter: string | null;
}
```

#### Parsing Strategy

The parser uses a line-by-line tokenization approach:

1. **Line Scanning**: Process input line by line, tracking position
2. **Indent Tracking**: Maintain indent stack for structure validation
3. **Token Recognition**: Identify keys, values, lists, multi-line strings
4. **Error Collection**: Accumulate all errors (continue after finding errors)

#### Key Validation Rules

| Rule | Validation | Error |
|------|------------|-------|
| Indentation | Consistent spaces (not mixed tabs/spaces) | "Inconsistent indentation" |
| Key Syntax | Valid key format before colon | "Invalid key syntax" |
| String Quotes | Matching quote pairs | "Unterminated string" |
| List Items | Proper dash-space prefix | "Invalid list item" |
| Document Markers | Valid --- and ... placement | "Invalid document marker" |
| Duplicate Keys | Same key at same level | "Duplicate key" |

#### Public API

```typescript
/**
 * Validate YAML syntax without fully parsing the document.
 * @param content - YAML content string
 * @returns ValidationResult with validity status and any errors
 */
export function validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;

/**
 * Validate YAML syntax for multi-document files.
 * @param content - YAML content string (may contain ---)
 * @returns ValidationResult with errors across all documents
 */
export function validateMultiDocYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;
```

### 3.2 CLI Module

#### Argument Structure

```typescript
// src/yaml-validator.ts

interface CliOptions {
  files: string[];
  quiet: boolean;
  help: boolean;
}

interface FileValidationResult {
  path: string;
  valid: boolean;
  errors: YamlError[];
  fileError?: string;  // For file access errors
}
```

#### Command Syntax

```
bun run validate-yaml [options] <file...>

Arguments:
  file...              YAML file paths or glob patterns

Options:
  -q, --quiet          Only output errors, suppress success messages
  -h, --help           Show help message

Exit Codes:
  0                    All files valid
  1                    One or more files have validation errors
  2                    Invalid arguments or file access errors
```

#### CLI Flow

```typescript
async function main(): Promise<void> {
  // 1. Parse arguments
  const options = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));

  if (options.help) {
    printHelp();
    process.exit(0);
  }

  if (options.files.length === 0) {
    console.error("Error: No files specified");
    printUsage();
    process.exit(2);
  }

  // 2. Resolve files (including globs)
  const resolvedFiles = await resolveFiles(options.files);

  if (resolvedFiles.length === 0) {
    console.error("Error: No files matched");
    process.exit(2);
  }

  // 3. Validate each file
  const results = await validateFiles(resolvedFiles);

  // 4. Output results
  outputResults(results, options.quiet);

  // 5. Exit with appropriate code
  const hasValidationErrors = results.some(r => !r.valid && !r.fileError);
  const hasFileErrors = results.some(r => r.fileError);

  if (hasFileErrors) {
    process.exit(2);
  } else if (hasValidationErrors) {
    process.exit(1);
  } else {
    process.exit(0);
  }
}
```

### 3.3 File Operations

#### File Reading

```typescript
async function readYamlFile(path: string): Promise<{ content?: string; error?: string }> {
  try {
    // Security: Validate path
    const normalizedPath = normalizePath(path);
    if (!isLocalPath(normalizedPath)) {
      return { error: "Only local file paths are allowed" };
    }

    const file = Bun.file(normalizedPath);

    if (!await file.exists()) {
      return { error: `File not found: ${path}` };
    }

    const content = await file.text();
    return { content };
  } catch (err) {
    return { error: `Cannot read file: ${err.message}` };
  }
}
```

#### Glob Resolution

```typescript
async function resolveGlob(pattern: string): Promise<string[]> {
  const glob = new Bun.Glob(pattern);
  const matches: string[] = [];

  for await (const path of glob.scan({ dot: false })) {
    if (path.endsWith('.yaml') || path.endsWith('.yml')) {
      matches.push(path);
    }
  }

  return matches;
}
```

### 3.4 Error Formatting

```typescript
function formatError(file: string, error: YamlError): string {
  return `${file}:${error.line}:${error.column}: ${error.message}`;
}

function formatFileError(file: string, message: string): string {
  return `${file}: ${message}`;
}

// Example output:
// config/app.yaml:15:3: Invalid indentation - expected 4 spaces, got 3
// config/db.yaml: File not found
```

### 3.5 Security Considerations

| Concern | Mitigation |
|---------|------------|
| Path Traversal | Normalize paths, reject paths with `..` outside working directory |
| Remote URLs | Check for protocol prefixes (http://, ftp://), reject non-local |
| File Size | Check file size before reading, reject files > 10MB |
| Content Execution | Parser only tokenizes, never evaluates content |

```typescript
function isLocalPath(path: string): boolean {
  // Reject URLs
  if (/^[a-z]+:\/\//i.test(path)) {
    return false;
  }

  // Resolve to absolute and check it's within allowed scope
  const resolved = resolve(path);
  const cwd = process.cwd();

  return resolved.startsWith(cwd) || !path.includes('..');
}
```

